            {
                "entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                "word": "koestal",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2dbb73e5-0f9f-414c-8ffe-a2f945300e19",
                        "entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "koestallen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
                        "entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "overdekte ruimte waarin koeien kunnen verblijven"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "veeteelt"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f53148ba-7890-4773-8102-6355aea1a493",
                                "sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
                                "text": "„Daarnaast”, weet SART-voorzitter Henk Vosmer, „hebben twee actieve boeren ons laten weten dat ze wat anders willen gaan doen met hun schuren. Ons is gevraagd de mogelijkheden voor het ombouwen naar ateliers te onderzoeken. De een stopt met het houden van varkens en de ander wil een koestal laten verplaatsen.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e8c9cc6-722c-47e2-b3c2-032d17422d6d",
                                "sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
                                "text": "Imponerend is ook de Kuhstall, in het Nederlands „koestal”. Het is een 11 meter hoge en 17 meter brede doorgang in een 24 meter dikke rotswand. De naam heeft eveneens met de Dertigjarige Oorlog te maken. Het was de plek waar de boeren hun vee voor de Zweedse soldaten verborgen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0016a458-0bc4-4b97-970d-dfb105880cf0",
                        "source_entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
                        "source_sense_description": "overdekte ruimte waarin koeien kunnen verblijven",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kuhstall",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kuhstall",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                        "entry_id": "8d7d7f7b-4bca-3424-bf1a-99b9a4c744dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gebäude einer Farm, eines landwirtschaftlichen Betriebs, das zur Unterbringung von Kühen dient"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e981801-e78f-425e-bb23-ab876625a761",
                                                "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                                "text": "Am Abend bringen wir die Kühe wieder in den Kuhstall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1acf77ce-d9b0-4510-a7fc-116b2e036443",
                                                "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                                "text": "„Sie rannten zu den Heuballen, die den rückwärtigen Eingang des Kuhstalls versperrten, und krochen dann so tief geduckt wie möglich zum Hühnerstall unter dem Küchenfenster.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11052dc1-4a3c-490b-940e-4fd5eb90ae2a",
                                                "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                                "text": "„Zwar wird Claudia von ihrer Amme getreulich versorgt, und ein neuer, energischer Kommandant hat im Kuhstall wieder eine bescheidene Herde zusammengebracht.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5555475c-f37e-47e6-86bf-cc02f2fe0492",
                                                "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                                "text": "„Der deutsche Quartierwirt guckte in Wams und Zipfelmütze, in der Hand die Mistgabel, mit der er den Kuhstall ausgemistet hatte, aus der Stalltür.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a689700a-a5d4-454b-85e0-d2a6e537ad34",
                                                "sense_id": "2683120a-6632-3f3c-9cfb-b4150ad946c3",
                                                "text": "„Die übrigen Notabeln seien: der Graf de Faverges, ehemals Abgeordneter, dessen Kuhställe musterhaft waren; der Bürgermeister, Monsieur Foureau, der mit Holz, Gips und allen möglichen Sachen handelte; ferner Monsieur Marescot, der Notar; der Abbé Jeufroy und die Witwe Bordin, die von ihren Zinsen lebe.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "53592f82-ba01-425b-a04c-571236806c18",
                        "source_entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
                        "source_sense_description": "overdekte ruimte waarin koeien kunnen verblijven",
                        "target_lang_word": "byre",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "byre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd2a28c1-c944-3875-a3f5-fe7e52253aaa",
                                        "entry_id": "14128257-bab5-3db1-a8ed-182ad9a2867e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A barn, especially one used for keeping cattle in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ef6e365-561b-47b8-8a02-2b708e5e7665",
                                                "sense_id": "cd2a28c1-c944-3875-a3f5-fe7e52253aaa",
                                                "text": "It was here in the kitchen, in the passage,\nIn the mews in the harn in the byre in the market-place [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e354f65-3959-4fac-b6ed-953d190f261b",
                                                "sense_id": "cd2a28c1-c944-3875-a3f5-fe7e52253aaa",
                                                "text": "’Children crawled over each other like little grey worms in the gutters,’ he said. ‘The only red things about them were their buttocks and they were raw. Their faces looked as if snails had slimed on them and their mothers were like great sick beasts whose byres had never been cleared.[…]’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2814b532-a937-4fd9-b881-ef812a39da2c",
                                                "sense_id": "cd2a28c1-c944-3875-a3f5-fe7e52253aaa",
                                                "text": "The visitors came up the narrow road through the forest from the south; they filled the spare-rooms, they bunked out in cow byres and barns."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d74345f8-fce8-4aa3-87f9-97b71a664729",
                        "source_entry_id": "5f123453-b970-3cac-914a-0a1edecafdcc",
                        "source_sense_id": "3b1ee9b6-7a70-3fe3-a950-8cc00b16f33c",
